# Line endings must not depend on each contributor's global git config.
#
# Git for Windows ships with core.autocrlf=true, which checks every text file
# out with CRLF. Shell scripts then break (`#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`), shellcheck
# fails on every one of them (SC1017), and marker files read with `cat`
# (.github/stacking-tool) stop comparing equal. The repository stores LF, so
# check out LF everywhere; text=auto still leaves binary files alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
